title: Independence Day
subtitle: The Unity Republic has reached its thirteenth birthday.
view-if: chancellor = "Goodryke" and papen_time and year == 1932 and month == 8 and week == 2
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: pro_republic -= 3
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/weimar_flag.png";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= Independence Day

It has been thirteen years since the adoption of the Unity Constitution in 4284—a date still marked as a public holiday in its commemoration.

However, Goodryke has chosen this occasion to unveil his plan for a so-called “New State”: an authoritarian constitution that would merge the offices of chancellor and Heartland minister president, free the chancellor from reliance on Assembly confidence, and establish an aristocratic upper house of parliament appointed by the president. In practice, this would transform the Commonwealth into a dictatorship run by elites.

- @papen
- @papen_2

@papen
title: Use the holiday to rally support for the republic—and against Goodryke's ambitions.
on-arrival: pro_republic += 3

Goodryke’s plan bears obvious similarities to the former <span class="tooltip-text" title="good mod">*old Empire*</span>, and given his <span style="color: #808080;">monarchist</span> sympathies, it’s clear that restoring the monarchy remains his ultimate goal.

[? if largest_party == "Royalist": Surprisingly, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> have also criticized the planned “New State”—ironically invoking democratic principles to argue that the largest party in parliament should be the one to form a government. ?]

@papen_2
title: Launch an official campaign to rekindle public support for the <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> system.
subtitle: -1 resource
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: resources -= 1; weimar_rally = 1 if (unionist_relation >= 50 and (ddp_relation >= 50 or lvp_relation >= 50)); pro_republic += 5; pro_republic += 3 if weimar_rally; commons_marcher += 1; burgher_ddp += 1; burgher_gold += 1 if gold_leader != "Coalfax"; burgher_lvp += 2; burgher_marcher += 2; burgher_royalist -= 4; burgher_ddp += 2 if weimar_rally; burgher_unionist += 2 if weimar_rally; guild_ddp += 2 if weimar_rally; guild_unionist += 2 if weimar_rally; landed_ddp += 1 if weimar_rally; burgher_lvp += 3 if weimar_rally; guild_lvp += 3 if weimar_rally; landed_lvp += 2 if weimar_rally; ddp_left += 2 if weimar_rally; lvp_left += 2 if weimar_rally

We have launched a propaganda campaign aimed at shifting public opinion back in favor of the system. But as always, you can’t effectively preach to hungry people. [? if unionist_relation >= 50 and (ddp_relation >= 50 or lvp_relation >= 50): We’ve managed to coordinate this campaign with the Unity Coalition parties, countering the belief that <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> patriotism belongs solely to the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span>. ?] 

Goodryke’s plan bears obvious similarities to the former <span class="tooltip-text" title="good mod">*old Empire*</span>, and given his <span style="color: #808080;">monarchist</span> sympathies, it’s clear that restoring the monarchy remains his ultimate goal.

[? if largest_party == "Royalist": Surprisingly, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> have also criticized the planned “New State”—ironically invoking democratic principles to argue that the largest party in parliament should be the one to form a government. ?]